# Description Rules

## When to add descriptions
1. Add descriptions for cvar and commands when user says work is completed ("работа завершена", "work is done", etc.)
2. Descriptions must be added in three places:
   - `assets/OSP2.cfg` (Russian)
   - `assets/OSP2English.cfg` (English)
   - `code/cgame/cg_cvardescriptions.c` (English with color codes)

## Cvar descriptions

### Location in cfg files
- Add cvar descriptions in `assets/OSP2.cfg` and `assets/OSP2English.cfg`
- Place descriptions after the `/belist` command (around line 18)
- NEW cvar descriptions MUST ALWAYS be added at the BEGINNING of that cvar block (immediately after `/belist`), not appended at the end
- Format: `seta cvar_name "value" // Description. 0 - disabled, 1 - enabled.`

### Style for cfg files
- Russian (OSP2.cfg): Short, clear description. Format: `// Описание. 0 - отключено, 1 - включено.`
- English (OSP2English.cfg): Short, clear description. Format: `// Description. 0 - disabled, 1 - enabled.`
- Include value meanings (0, 1, 2, etc.) when applicable
- Mention requirements (e.g., "Requires vid_restart", "Требует vid_restart")
- For bitmasks, explain each bit value
- For color values, mention format: `<color> - name, digit or hex`

### Location in cg_cvardescriptions.c
- Add NEW entries ALWAYS at the end of `cvarDescriptionTable[]` array (before closing brace)
- Format: `{ "cvar_name", "Description with color codes" },`

### Style for cg_cvardescriptions.c
- Use color codes: `^2` (green), `^3` (yellow), `^4` (blue), `^5` (cyan), `^6` (magenta), `^7` (white)
- Format: `"Description. Set ^20^7 to disable."`
- For bitmasks, use format:
  ```
  "Description. Bitmask:\n  ^20^7 - disabled\n  ^21^7 - enabled\n  ^22^7 - option2"
  ```
- Reference other cvars with: `^3cvar_name^7`
- Include examples: `\"^2example^7\"`
- Use `\n` for line breaks
- Mention requirements: `Requires ^3other_cvar^7 ^21^7`

## Command descriptions

### Location in cfg files
- Add command descriptions in `assets/OSP2.cfg` and `assets/OSP2English.cfg`
- Place in the "//// Дополнительные команды" section at the very bottom of the file (after line 325)
- NEW command descriptions MUST ALWAYS be added at the BEGINNING of that section (top of the command list), not at the end
- Format: `// /command_name // Description`

### Style for command descriptions
- Russian (OSP2.cfg): `// /command_name // Описание команды.`
- English (OSP2English.cfg): `// /command_name // Command description.`
- If command takes arguments, mention them: `// /command <arg> // Description. Use <arg> to...`
- Keep descriptions concise but informative

## Examples

### Cvar in cfg (Russian):
```
seta cg_snow "1" // Эффект снега. 0 - отключено, 1 - включено. Требует vid_restart.
```

### Cvar in cfg (English):
```
seta cg_snow "1" // Enable snow particle effect. 0 - disabled, 1 - enabled. Requires vid_restart.
```

### Cvar in cg_cvardescriptions.c:
```
{ "cg_snow", "Enable snow particle effect. Set ^20^7 to disable. Requires ^3vid_restart^7." },
```

### Command in cfg (Russian):
```
// /belist // Выводит список команд добавленных в BE в консоль.
```

### Command in cfg (English):
```
// /belist // Displays the list of BE-added commands in the console.
```

## Important notes
- Always maintain consistency with existing descriptions
- Use same terminology as existing descriptions
- For bitmasks, always explain all bit values
- For color parameters, always mention format options
- Check existing descriptions to match style exactly



